# Slash commands (type `/` in chat)

| Command | Action |
|---------|--------|
| `/push` | Commit current progress with a readable English message, then push to the **current branch’s upstream** (e.g. `dev` → `origin/dev`) |
| `/pack` | Run `bash scripts/package.sh` → `dist/Ask_AI_Plugin_vX.Y.Z.zip` (excludes tests/scripts/docs/dev trees) |
| `/upgrade-version` | Bump version per `.cursor/rules/version-update.mdc` (alias: `/version-up`) |

When the user invokes one of these (via slash command or by saying the same intent), follow the matching prompt in `.cursor/commands/<name>.md` exactly.

- `/upgrade-version` → `.cursor/commands/upgrade-version.md`
- `/version-up` → same workflow (see `.cursor/commands/version-up.md` alias)
- `/pack` → `.cursor/commands/pack.md` (must use `scripts/package.sh`, stay aligned with `.gitignore` packaging notes)
- `/push` → `.cursor/commands/push.md`

## Commit message style for `/push`

Use clear English with connecting words (not telegraphic keyword stacks), e.g. “Add … after …”, “Fix … when …”.

## Defaults

- Push target: **current branch’s upstream**; if none, `git push -u origin HEAD`. On `dev`, expect `origin/dev`.
- Never force-push unless the user explicitly asks.
- `/upgrade-version` does not commit or pack unless combined with `/push` / `/pack`.
